# core v3.10 — NEGATIVE. A consent scope whose value is not a consent scope.
#
# The value here, cascade:SelfReported, is a REAL term: a cascade:DataProvenance
# subclass declared in core.ttl since v1. That is the whole point of choosing
# it. A fixture that put an invented IRI in this position would be rejected by
# any constraint at all, including one that merely checked the value resolved;
# an IRI that exists in the same namespace and is simply not a member of the
# closed cascade:ConsentScope code list is rejected only by the constraint this
# release added -- cascade:ConsentScopeShape / cascade:consentScope / sh:in.
# It is also the confusion a producer will actually make, since provenance is
# the other cascade: code list a record of this shape carries.
#
# WHY THIS IS THE ONLY NEGATIVE THIS RELEASE ADMITS. There is no fixture here
# asserting that a MISSING consent scope is rejected, because core v3.10
# requires the property nowhere and is not meant to. That is ratchet step 2 --
# sh:minCount 1 at sh:Warning on clinical:SocialHistoryRecordShape, once a
# reference producer emits the predicate -- and it belongs to a later vocabulary
# version.
#
# WHAT THE POLARITY SUFFIX IS CATCHING. Against the previous pin (spec 9b13ae4,
# core v3.8) no shape anywhere mentions consent, so this file and its VALID
# sibling are indistinguishable and this one passes. .INVALID.ttl is what turns
# that silence into a reported NO_VIOLATION.
#
# Everything else on this record is valid, so exactly one constraint rejects it:
# sh:InConstraintComponent on cascade:consentScope.
#
# Fully synthetic.

@prefix cascade: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/core/v1#> .
@prefix clinical: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/clinical/v1#> .
@prefix health: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/health/v1#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<urn:cascade:social-history:example-consent-scope-wrong-value>
    a clinical:SocialHistoryRecord ;
    clinical:socialHistoryCategory "smokingStatus" ;
    health:smokingStatus "never" ;

    # THE DEFECT: a cascade:DataProvenance individual where a
    # cascade:ConsentScope individual belongs.
    cascade:consentScope cascade:SelfReported ;

    cascade:dataProvenance cascade:EHRVerified .
